  "step_2": "The individual in the verbal report expresses a preference for the safe option (Lottery B) — winning exactly 2400 Euros with certainty — over the uncertain option (Lottery A), which has a maximum of 2500 Euros but a risk of getting nothing. The individual states that the difference of only 100 Euros was sufficient to justify choosing the safe option. The deliberation focuses on risk and certainty, emphasizing the value of a guaranteed outcome over a risky one with a small chance of a higher payoff. There is no mention of skewness, distribution of probabilities, or any analysis of how much probability is assigned to favorable versus unfavorable outcomes. The justification is based solely on risk aversion and the perceived value of certainty, not on skewness.",
